[{:db/id "q-333105/selection/91339d565a272a7fced8fd8e1e056ce3648a570328ed62937380470b9024998a" :answer/id #uuid "a42303f7-0d09-5502-b0ae-9ced5f9cc56d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=-{y}_{\\text{new}}+y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333105/selection/a9caa1009e69128116663e386c55f90567413afac2d6561dadb646d1e800e76a" :answer/id #uuid "b83c8bcb-15ac-59ae-92e3-33db5021e93a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-y-{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333105/selection/9b077fda6c1f492659a9470e18b3d8d3d5d0b109a0facd75e432886b66b2f781" :answer/id #uuid "3cd44607-79c3-5421-916f-a4d02e3d47fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333105/selection/741b547ec4ea5095f0985c19aceb63b37ed3e188b7eeece2c5a3c3a3ebf00b07" :answer/id #uuid "90fb1a44-20f8-535d-b1ee-9b00d537ac30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=-\\,y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333105/selection/e5664f78ea6fc2e40b9ca636b4278c20c7dcd894f37b93cadfa11b0762ca9a9e" :answer/id #uuid "b86a3758-3dd5-53da-b15e-0089d9bcc1e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=-\\,y-0.5{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333105/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a60dc863-e46e-5888-a139-a1ce74c38570" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-333105/selection/741b547ec4ea5095f0985c19aceb63b37ed3e188b7eeece2c5a3c3a3ebf00b07" :answer-field/choices ["q-333105/selection/91339d565a272a7fced8fd8e1e056ce3648a570328ed62937380470b9024998a" "q-333105/selection/a9caa1009e69128116663e386c55f90567413afac2d6561dadb646d1e800e76a" "q-333105/selection/9b077fda6c1f492659a9470e18b3d8d3d5d0b109a0facd75e432886b66b2f781" "q-333105/selection/741b547ec4ea5095f0985c19aceb63b37ed3e188b7eeece2c5a3c3a3ebf00b07" "q-333105/selection/e5664f78ea6fc2e40b9ca636b4278c20c7dcd894f37b93cadfa11b0762ca9a9e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333105" :question/id #uuid "3e1fd1e0-f9ee-5efd-85cc-903531185842" :question/math-academy-id "q-333105" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}+2y,\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $Δx=0.5,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **general form** of $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ in terms of the new values ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and the current value $y?$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+2{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side to define $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {{{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.5$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=-\\,y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-333105/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6329ab32-968f-5041-b2e3-12dde408968a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333105"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333106/selection/32632dac4469ea0ae8f540ad262dc504ca1bf51d170f49af40ebe3933705ec38" :answer/id #uuid "20f2d2e9-2c6b-544b-ab13-60ecc8dda21d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.75{y}^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333106/selection/d06c14796be55f71204d1679fd2a213286c8128f820417cc5e2f07c29df3bd07" :answer/id #uuid "5b17a757-9b05-51ca-a525-914441c169b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=-{y}_{\\text{new}}+y+2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}-0.75{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333106/selection/9c2f5ad838bcde88e9f796d2d2c3b361cd50427f82cdb6f44a2decd4c7614473" :answer/id #uuid "49c5784c-45a1-5808-99b3-07a0be60061f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-{y}_{\\text{new}}+2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}-y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333106/selection/ca9dd692e9f3b2c58b0f0fcb169cba1d0e167b16fef59c7df5ff48c214daa8e3" :answer/id #uuid "e7c59e9e-e062-5d3b-aaeb-06eab3a729e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333106/selection/4cc9bcb41c262b5c004831101d46388d5b3e4cb058245121ac3bca0373dafd56" :answer/id #uuid "f3ed478c-35c9-5a77-a22c-cb37781cdf64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-y-2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}-0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333106/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e0bad87-84b4-5281-80dc-e882a31ec666" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-333106/selection/ca9dd692e9f3b2c58b0f0fcb169cba1d0e167b16fef59c7df5ff48c214daa8e3" :answer-field/choices ["q-333106/selection/32632dac4469ea0ae8f540ad262dc504ca1bf51d170f49af40ebe3933705ec38" "q-333106/selection/d06c14796be55f71204d1679fd2a213286c8128f820417cc5e2f07c29df3bd07" "q-333106/selection/9c2f5ad838bcde88e9f796d2d2c3b361cd50427f82cdb6f44a2decd4c7614473" "q-333106/selection/ca9dd692e9f3b2c58b0f0fcb169cba1d0e167b16fef59c7df5ff48c214daa8e3" "q-333106/selection/4cc9bcb41c262b5c004831101d46388d5b3e4cb058245121ac3bca0373dafd56"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333106" :question/id #uuid "43774789-c34c-506f-b225-3746f175168c" :question/math-academy-id "q-333106" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3x-{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=2\n$$\n\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $Δx=0.75,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **general form** of $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ in terms of the new values ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and the current value $y?$" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(3{x}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2})\\cdot 0.75 \\\\  & =2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}-0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side to define $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}-0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2} \\\\ {{0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.75$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.75({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-2.25{x}_{\\text{new}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-333106/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6329ab32-968f-5041-b2e3-12dde408968a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333106"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333119/selection/ea898f42b1b74422918209c32e57ffb09c02f45b0152d6f302b67e5b85e89da9" :answer/id #uuid "3cd37958-a241-5be2-93db-638dee95d3c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-0.125{y}_{\\text{new}}-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333119/selection/7ecf52ab9abe9cd521725b5858b9f1d6a7bf3e4d31daa84b05c64307055fe02b" :answer/id #uuid "6612eba8-2d17-58e6-8790-ad600d8fa2fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-0.125{y}_{\\text{new}}+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333119/selection/b1bde6e2bf2d76e592b2d4fa35e15a5287fd2b181709b3c318cf152362e700f9" :answer/id #uuid "6d82e815-6e4d-5d4d-a346-e460c1dca513" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=-0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-0.125{y}_{\\text{new}}-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333119/selection/9188d6e12907c47d8619dd77c5a3819347f3419404d3d6667ad49129228a162f" :answer/id #uuid "c0208d98-3904-543c-a806-fa2b9424513c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333119/selection/2dfcffc304eb20f6749e1daef4a998b925173cc8181bd71c77022cd41eb44f49" :answer/id #uuid "2c3f12c2-c0b0-5daf-90f4-e479d78ca368" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-0.125{y}_{\\text{new}}-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333119/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e0186698-e195-518a-9289-0b65d688ae25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-333119/selection/2dfcffc304eb20f6749e1daef4a998b925173cc8181bd71c77022cd41eb44f49" :answer-field/choices ["q-333119/selection/ea898f42b1b74422918209c32e57ffb09c02f45b0152d6f302b67e5b85e89da9" "q-333119/selection/7ecf52ab9abe9cd521725b5858b9f1d6a7bf3e4d31daa84b05c64307055fe02b" "q-333119/selection/b1bde6e2bf2d76e592b2d4fa35e15a5287fd2b181709b3c318cf152362e700f9" "q-333119/selection/9188d6e12907c47d8619dd77c5a3819347f3419404d3d6667ad49129228a162f" "q-333119/selection/2dfcffc304eb20f6749e1daef4a998b925173cc8181bd71c77022cd41eb44f49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333119" :question/id #uuid "4acdd86e-feb2-5b8f-9158-a782834e3029" :question/math-academy-id "q-333119" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}y-{y}^{3},\\,y(1)=3\n$$\n\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $Δx=0.5,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **specific function** $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ used in the first step?" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3})\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side and define the resulting expression as $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3} \\\\ {{0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-y}_{⏟}}_{g({y}_{\\text{new}})} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.5$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-y.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+0.5=1.5.$ Therefore, the function used in the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-0.5\\cdot (1.5)^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}-3 \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-1.125{y}_{\\text{new}}-3 \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{3}-0.125{y}_{\\text{new}}-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-333119/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6329ab32-968f-5041-b2e3-12dde408968a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333119"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333293/field-1/e2e7cbb360d74ff41cef3115192e100ecb5f4806f63f264ec83419c951763afc" :answer/id #uuid "a36092b9-0d69-51bc-80f8-e813b6b6e88b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.65" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333293/field-1/2b2071f6ce0dc41b4833648ad1b1860b4f28e546e6156a589085df2d460729d3" :answer/id #uuid "02eb2b7c-6285-5949-bebc-240ddfbbcec9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333293/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3cd54c34-cdff-5b54-b61f-3c9c69381425" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333293/field-1/e2e7cbb360d74ff41cef3115192e100ecb5f4806f63f264ec83419c951763afc" :answer-field/choices ["q-333293/field-1/e2e7cbb360d74ff41cef3115192e100ecb5f4806f63f264ec83419c951763afc" "q-333293/field-1/2b2071f6ce0dc41b4833648ad1b1860b4f28e546e6156a589085df2d460729d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333293" :question/id #uuid "2b04598d-7f01-5a4d-adbb-3db42072dfa0" :question/math-academy-id "q-333293" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,y(1.5)=1\n$$\n\nUse the implicit Euler method with one step and Newton's method to approximate $y(2).$ Round your answer to two decimal places.\n\n$y(2)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nSince we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=2,$ we will use a step size of\n\n$$\nΔx=2-1.5=0.5.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2})\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and move all terms to the left-hand side and define the resulting expression as $g({y}_{\\text{new}}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the equation\n\n$$\n0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=0.5$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-y-0.5({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1.5+0.5=2.$ Then, the function $g$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-1-0.5(2)^{2} \\\\  & =0.5({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+{y}_{\\text{new}}-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use a root-finding method with starting point $y=1$ to solve $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0.$ We'll use Newton's method. \n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{g({y}_{\\text{new}})}{{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})}\n$$\n\nNote that the derivative of $g$ is\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}({y}_{\\text{new}})=({y}_{\\text{new}})+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton's method iterative scheme is as follows:\n\n$$\n({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n+1}=({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-\\frac{0.5(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})^{2}+({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n}-3}{(({y}_{\\text{new}})_{n})+1}\n$$\n\nApplying several iterations of Newton's method starting with $y(1.5)=1,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({y}_{\\text{new}})_{1} & =1 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{2} & =1.750000 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{3} & ≈1.647727 \\\\ ({y}_{\\text{new}})_{4} & ≈1.645752\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(2)≈1.65,$ rounded to two decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-333293/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "866481fb-c460-5a39-a7a0-84b64d8bd673"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333293"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
